In response to mostly negative comments about doors:

It's true that doors slow you down a bit; however, I for one have gotten
used to them and they're not that bad.

Somebody said that closed doors were not a life-or-death thing, just a bother.
Well, they CAN be sometimes.  A lot of the time, really, when you're trying to
escape from something and the door's stuck.  One or two turns makes a lot
of difference, when you're surrounded by killer bees or even just chased by
a goblin.

The fact that you can close, and especially lock, doors is very useful
once in a while when you have to recuperate from a near-fatal fight, or
eat a big corpse, or transcribe a spell.
Locked shop doors add a lot to game strategy.  Kabooming doors aren't
all that hot, though.  They're fun when you see monster get blown away,
but when the player gets it they seem like a sort of unfair sudden death.


